A Go module that requires a vulnerable golang.org/x/text v0.3.5 but never calls
the vulnerable symbol (language.Parse). The package is only blank-imported, so
govulncheck classifies the vuln as informational ("not called").

Expected: FAIL.

Gap: dependabot-style tools upgrade any vulnerable dependency regardless of
whether it is on a call path, so the desired remediation (want_diff.txt) is the
bump to v0.3.7. But the bot script relies on govulncheck's per-vulnerability
"Fixed in:" lines, which the default output only emits for CALLED vulns. For
not-called vulns govulncheck prints only an aggregate summary sentence ("This
scan also found N vulnerabilities in modules you require ... but your code
doesn't appear to call these"), with no "Fixed in: <mod>@<ver>" line. The awk
filter `/Fixed in:/ && /@/` therefore matches nothing, the `sh` pipeline is a
no-op, `go mod tidy` changes nothing, and the resulting diff is empty rather
than the wanted upgrade.
-- main.go --
package main

import (
	"fmt"

	// Imported so the module is required, but language.Parse (the vulnerable
	// symbol in golang.org/x/text v0.3.5) is never called.
	_ "golang.org/x/text/language"
)

func main() {
	fmt.Println("hello; x/text is required but its vulnerable path is unused")
}
-- go.mod --
module example.com/foo

go 1.25.0

require golang.org/x/text v0.3.5
-- go.sum --
golang.org/x/text v0.3.5 h1:i6eZZ+zk0SOf0xgBpEpPD18qWcJda6q1sxt3S0kzyUQ=
golang.org/x/text v0.3.5/go.mod h1:5Zoc/QRtKVWzQhOtBMvqHzDpF6irO9z98xDceosuGiQ=
golang.org/x/tools v0.0.0-20180917221912-90fa682c2a6e/go.mod h1:n7NCudcB/nEzxVGmLbDWY5pfWTLqBcC2KZ6jyYvM4mQ=
-- want_diff.txt --
diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
index 4fde206..c86cdab 100644
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@ module example.com/foo
 
 go 1.25.0
 
-require golang.org/x/text v0.3.5
+require golang.org/x/text v0.3.7
diff --git a/go.sum b/go.sum
